OpenPCDet (Apache License 2.0)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
This repository is based on OpenPCDet v0.6.0
(https://github.com/open-mmlab/OpenPCDet), Copyright (c) OpenMMLab /
OpenPCDet Development Team. The full Apache-2.0 license text is in LICENSE.
Original OpenPCDet file headers are retained in the corresponding sources.

Modifications and additions in this repository include (non-exhaustive):
  - MambaVoxelBlock and integration into the sparse VoxelNeXt-style backbone
    (pcdet/models/backbones_3d/mamba_voxel_block.py and related wiring)
  - RCS point-feature controls (MODEL.RCS_IN_INPUT) and optional RCS-aware
    BEV modules used for Table 7 ablations
  - Paper experiment configs under tools/cfgs/, analysis scripts under
    tools/analysis/, and documentation under docs/
  - Checkpoint loading adaptations for spconv weight layouts used by the
    released Radar M3-Net / 4D-MambaNet weights
  - Dataset path overrides via MAMBANET4D_DATA / DATA_PATH

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Radar M3-Net components (released with permission)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
MSVFE / multi-scale VFE, temporal fusion, sparse dual-head detection, and
related VoD/TJ4D dataset helpers derive from Radar M3-Net
(Y. Yang et al., Expert Systems with Applications, 2025, vol. 286, 127515).
Files taken from that codebase are marked with a permission header.
See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Point Transformer V3 / Pointcept (MIT License)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PTv3 attention stages and Point structures are adapted from Pointcept
(https://github.com/Pointcept/Pointcept), MIT License. Original author
headers are retained under pcdet/models/backbones_3d/attn_layer/ptv3/ and
pcdet/models/model_utils/pointcept_utils/.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Other third-party dependencies
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Training and inference additionally use mamba-ssm (Apache-2.0) and
causal-conv1d (BSD-3-Clause). See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and requirements.
